# rsync exclude patterns for the public snapshot.
#
# actions/checkout only materializes tracked files, so anything already in
# .gitignore will not be present anyway. Listing those paths here regardless is
# deliberate: it makes the filter correct when run locally against a dirty
# working tree, and it survives a file being accidentally committed later.
#
# Patterns are rsync filter rules, not gitignore rules. A trailing / matches
# directories only; a leading / anchors to the repo root.

# Never publish VCS or CI-local state
.git/
.github/public-README.md

# Agent / editor state
.claude/
# Registers the wedding-hq MCP endpoint for Claude Code sessions started here.
# No secrets in it -- the Access token comes from the environment -- but it
# points at a private planning tool and is useless to anyone without that
# token, so it is advice to nobody on the mirror. Root-anchored.
/.mcp.json
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Working notes for agents. Tracked, unlike .claude/, because it is worth having
# in the history and reviewable in a PR -- but held back from the mirror for now
# rather than published as advice to nobody. Root-anchored: this is the one at
# the top of the repo, not any CLAUDE.md that later appears in a subdirectory.
/CLAUDE.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Guest data. This is the reason this repo is mirrored rather than published.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The whole directory, not named files.
#
# data/kerala-trip-responses.json (since deleted) held 43 real email addresses with room
# pairings and a price exception. data/schedule-events.json is the plaintext
# that every gated event's copy is encrypted from -- its own header says it is
# never imported by src/ precisely so that private copy never reaches the
# browser unencrypted, and publishing it hands over exactly what the encryption
# exists to withhold, for all ten gated events.
#
# The first version of this file named kerala-trip-responses.json alone and let
# schedule-events.json through. Excluding the directory is the rule that would
# not have made that mistake: everything in data/ is generator input, none of it
# is needed to read the code, and the next file added here is private by default
# rather than by someone remembering to add a line.
data/

# Working plans. Tracked and reviewable in a PR, like CLAUDE.md above, but a
# plan for anything touching rooming or the roster is mostly a list of which
# real person maps to which roster row and who shares a room with whom, and it
# is only useful if it says so. Sanitizing that into scientists would leave the
# next agent re-deriving it against the live sheet, which is the work the plan
# exists to save. Held back as a directory for the same reason data/ is: the
# next plan is private by default. Root-anchored, so a docs/plans/ that later
# appears somewhere else is not silently swept up with it.
/docs/plans/

# Guest data exports, mirroring the .gitignore block of the same name.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv

# Local secrets. The glob rather than the two exact-ish patterns below it used
# to be, which between them still missed a stray `.envn` -- a full copy of .env,
# private key and admin passphrase included. Anything starting with .env is a
# credential until proven otherwise.
.env*

# Build output and local state
dist/
dist-server/
deployment.log
working-material/

# Not present in CI, where checkout only materializes tracked files, but a
# local dry run copies the whole dependency tree without this.
node_modules/
